						split: 'the focus ring is breaking only where it overflows a tight layout; the selected-row fill is preference. The popup row also lost its fixed `height: 40px` and is now built from `padding-block: $token-scale-200` around a 24px line box — the same 40px, but sourced from padding. Any app rule setting `padding` on that row as a **shorthand** now zeroes the block value and flattens the row to a bare line of text; rewrite it as `padding-inline` alone. The popup also shrank and got rounder: `max-height` went from a hard `300px` to `--osui-dropdown-list-max-height: 240px`, and the radius from `--border-radius-soft` (4px in classic) to `--border-radius-lg` (8px). A list that fit without scrolling can now scroll — restore with `--osui-dropdown-list-max-height` and `--osui-dropdown-popup-border-radius`, using a **literal** for the radius, since `--border-radius-soft` itself is no longer 4px.',
